  "id": "COMPOUND:34435 - PROTEIN:4022",
  "verbalization": "Ent-Gloeosteretriol appears to interact with Proteasome subunit alpha type-7 through multiple distinct pathways, each involving different targets. The first pathway links Ent-Gloeosteretriol to Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK, which is then targeted by Oblonganoside C, and finally by Proteasome subunit alpha type-7. The second pathway connects Ent-Gloeosteretriol to DMS-53, which is targeted by Gerontoisoflavone A, also leading to the same proteasome subunit. The third pathway involves Ent-Gloeosteretriol targeting Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, which is ultimately targeted by a complex compound that also affects the proteasome subunit. These interactions suggest that Ent-Gloeosteretriol may modulate proteasome activity through various molecular mechanisms, potentially influencing protein degradation processes. The evidence supports a role for Ent-Gloeosteretriol in interacting with the proteasome, though the exact mechanism by which it affects the subunit remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores indicate a consistent but not absolute relationship, highlighting the need for further experimental validation.",
